# Line-art reference project

- Treat `.cursor/demo/line-art-style-magic-cabin-main/` as the primary reference for this project's visual language, procedural models, animation feel, and Three.js implementation patterns.
- Before implementing or revising a visual feature, inspect the matching implementation in `.cursor/demo/line-art-style-magic-cabin-main/index.html` when one exists.
- Preserve the reference's core line-art method: a filled mesh paired with `THREE.EdgesGeometry` and `THREE.LineSegments`.
- Match the reference's restrained paper-toned palette, dark geometry outlines, low-poly shapes, soft transparency, and playful deformation where appropriate.
- Adapt reference code into the project's modular TypeScript structure; do not copy unrelated systems into one file.
- Keep all adapted procedural geometry under `src/models/`, controllers under their own subsystem, and animation behavior separate from scene composition.
- When an exact match conflicts with the current project's networking, Scene lifecycle, CommonUI stack, or maintainability rules, preserve the visual behavior while integrating through the existing architecture.
